= Imported vocabulary =

This administrative semantic category groups pages that expose vocabulary imported from external ontologies or namespace mappings rather than predicates designed natively by BITwiki.

== Purpose ==

Imported vocabulary exists for interoperability. Membership here signals that a Property or related semantic surface inherits meaning from an external vocabulary and should be interpreted with that vocabulary's definitions and import mapping in view.

Current examples include FOAF and OWL properties recovered from the live BITwiki Semantic MediaWiki configuration.

== Boundary ==

This category is '''not''' a knowledge Domain and does not imply that imported terms become part of BITwiki's native ontology merely because they are available to SMW.

Before using an imported predicate in canonical V2 content:

* verify the corresponding <code>MediaWiki:Smw import ...</code> mapping;
* preserve the external predicate's intended semantics;
* prefer a V2-native Property when BITwiki needs materially different semantics;
* document any deliberate alignment or translation rather than silently treating similarly named predicates as equivalent.

